.TH PCHART 1 2026-11-03 pchart "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pchart \- project charts in the terminal that check themselves
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pchart
.RI [ PLAN ]
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B pchart
.I COMMAND PLAN
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-today
.IR DATE ]
.RB [ \-\-holidays
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B pchart help
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pchart
plans projects as roadmaps, Gantt charts and milestone charts, in the terminal, and checks them while
you change them.
It answers three questions first: does the date hold, who waits on whom, and what is next.
.PP
A plan is one text file, the plan file, usually ending in
.IR .pchart .
It is the only source of truth: every picture, PDF, SVG and Markdown file pChart writes is output
and can be made again from it.
pChart saves every change at once and
.B u
takes it back.
It never moves a fixed date on its own and never changes a plan behind your back; it warns instead.
.PP
pChart speaks plainly: the chain that
.I decides the date
instead of the critical path, what an item has
.I to spare
instead of float, and what it
.I waits on
instead of its dependencies.
.PP
Without
.I PLAN
pChart starts: it offers the templates for a new plan, the plans opened before and, in a workspace,
the projects of the team.
With a
.I COMMAND
it answers on the command line, for people and for agents; with
.B \-\-json
every answer is machine\-readable.
.SH SCREENS
The screens sit as tabs in the title bar.
.TP
.B Start
The templates (New application, Website relaunch, Product launch, Empty plan), the plans opened
before, and in a workspace its projects with how each stands, a preview of the chosen one and what
to look at in it.
.TP
.B 1 Situation
Where the plan stands: the verdict on the target date and how many working days it has to spare,
what changed since the last snapshot, what is next, and the chain that decides the date.
.TP
.B 2 Roadmap
The swimlane roadmap: a lane for each team, the phases above, milestones in the theme's accent,
and the chain that decides the date.
It has three levels, Overview, Standard and Full.
Here the plan is changed.
Before every piece of work has a length, this screen is the network of what waits on what instead.
.TP
.B 3 Checks
Problems, warnings and hints, by weight, each with what it means and what to do.
.TP
.B 4 Export
A view for others, its audience and its formats; the preview is exactly the file.
.TP
.B 5 People
How full each team and each person is, week by week across the projects of the workspace.
Outside a workspace it shows the people the plan names.
.TP
.B 6 Reports
In a workspace: what the team reports about the plan, and what taking a report would do.
.TP
.B Present mode
The situation for a meeting, one statement a screen and large: where we stand, the chain that
decides the date, who waits on whom, what is next, and the roadmap at the Overview level.
.SH KEYS
.SS Everywhere
.TP
.B 1\(en6
Situation, Roadmap, Checks, Export, People, Reports.
.TP
.B Tab
The next screen;
.B Shift+Tab
the one before.
.TP
.B ?
Explain this screen: what it answers, its keys and its symbols.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Find any action by typing what you want, such as
.I move launch
or
.IR pdf .
.TP
.B o
The projects of the workspace, a new plan or another one.
.TP
.B F5
Present the situation in a meeting.
.TP
.B u
Undo the last change.
.TP
.B q
Quit; every change is saved already.
.PP
When a window is too narrow for every key hint, the hints first use shorter words, and then
.B ? all keys
says that there are more.
.SS Situation
.TP
.B \(ua\(da
Choose a step of
.IR Next .
.TP
.B Enter
Show it in the roadmap.
.TP
.B c
What changed since the last snapshot, on the roadmap.
.TP
.B t
Keep a snapshot of how the plan stands today.
.SS Roadmap
.TP
.B \(ua\(da
Choose an item; at the Overview level a lane.
.TP
.B \(<-\(->
Try the item longer or shorter, as a what\-if;
.B Enter
keeps it,
.B Esc
discards it.
.TP
.B Enter
Change when it starts: after what it waits on, on a fixed date, no earlier than or no later than a
date.
.TP
.B y
Why this date: the items that set it.
.TP
.B a
Add work or a milestone after the item, or before the milestone the plan ends with.
.TP
.B r
Rename the item and its lane.
.TP
.B w
Choose what the item waits on.
.TP
.B x
Remove the item.
.TP
.B p
Choose who does it and the share of their time it takes; or type the name of someone new.
.TP
.B s
Report how it is going, in a workspace.
.TP
.B Space
Show or hide the details beside the roadmap; they need 150 columns.
.TP
.B n
Add notes to items and to days of a lane;
.B i
marks a milestone important.
.TP
.B t
Keep a snapshot.
.TP
.B c
Show the roadmap with the dates of the last snapshot dashed.
.TP
.B d
Overview, Standard or Full.
.SS Network
Before every piece of work has a length, the second screen shows how the plan is built.
.TP
.B \(ua\(da\(<-\(->
Choose an item.
.TP
.B Enter
Give it a length.
.TP
.B a
Add an item after it.
.TP
.B r
Rename it.
.TP
.B w
Choose what it waits on.
.TP
.B x
Remove it.
.SS Checks
.TP
.B \(ua\(da
Choose a check.
.TP
.B Enter
Show it in the roadmap.
.TP
.B b
Add the buffer a missing one asks for.
.SS Export
.TP
.B \(ua\(da
The view, the audience or the formats.
.TP
.B \(<-\(->
Change it.
.TP
.B Space
Switch a format on or off.
.TP
.B Enter
Write the files to
.I export/
next to the plan.
.TP
.B Esc
Back to the situation.
.SS People
.TP
.B \(ua\(da
Choose a person; teams are headings with their sum for each week.
.TP
.B \(<-\(->
Choose a week.
.TP
.B Enter
Outside a workspace: make the plan's folder a team, with the people the plan names.
.SS Reports
.TP
.B \(ua\(da
Choose a report.
.TP
.B Enter
Take it into the plan, as one change that
.B u
takes back.
.TP
.B e
Change it first, then take it.
.TP
.B x
Decline it; the plan stays as it is.
.SS Present mode
.TP
.B \(<-\(->
The slide before or after; also
.BR "Page Up" ,
.BR "Page Down" ,
.B Home
and
.BR End .
.TP
.B \(ua\(da
Choose an entry of the slide: a step, a handoff or a piece of work.
.TP
.B Space
Show or hide its details.
.TP
.B Esc
Back to pChart;
.B F5
too.
.SH COMMANDS
Items and lanes are named by their ids in the plan file.
Dates are
.IR YYYY\-MM\-DD .
.TP
.BR "pchart " [ \fIPLAN\fR ] " " [ \-\-theme " \fINAME\fR]"
Open the plan in the terminal, in the colours of the current Omarchy theme, which it follows while it
changes, or in Labra without Omarchy.
.B \-\-theme
takes a theme by name instead, such as
.I labra
or
.IR harbor .
Without
.I PLAN
it starts: a new plan from a template, written to this folder, or a plan opened before.
.TP
.BI "pchart new " PLAN " \-\-template " ID " \fR[\fB\-\-name \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-target \fIDATE \fR| \fB\-\-start \fIDATE \fR| \fB\-\-no\-dates\fR]"
Write a new plan from a template:
.IR new\-application ,
.IR website\-relaunch ,
.I product\-launch
or
.IR empty .
.B \-\-target
puts the date on its last milestone and plans backwards from it,
.B \-\-start
plans forwards from it; without either it starts today.
.B \-\-no\-dates
keeps only how it is built: the work without lengths, so the plan has no dates until each has one.
Never writes over a file.
.TP
.B pchart list
The projects of the workspace pChart runs in, each with how it stands, and the people to look at:
over their capacity, or away during their work.
.TP
.BI "pchart report " "PLAN ITEM " "\fR(\fB\-\-done \fR| \fB\-\-on\-track \fR| \fB\-\-risk \fR| \fB\-\-later \fIDAYS\fR) [\fB\-\-comment \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-by \fINAME\fR]"
Say how a piece of work stands, for the project lead: done, on track, at risk, or needing
.I DAYS
working days more.
It goes to the workspace's
.I reports/
folder as a file of its own; the plan stays as it is until the project lead takes it.
.B \-\-by
names who reports, else
.BR PCHART_NAME .
.TP
.BI "pchart reports " PLAN
The reports about the plan, newest first: who says what, whether it is answered, and what taking it
would do.
.TP
.BI "pchart snapshot " PLAN " \fR[\fB\-\-name \fINAME\fR]"
Keep how the plan stands today at the end of the plan file: what the chain has to spare and the dates
of every item.
.TP
.BI "pchart diff " PLAN " \fR[\fB\-\-since \fIDATE\fR]"
What changed since the last snapshot, or the last one up to
.IR DATE :
what the chain has to spare, work that got longer or shorter, new and removed items, moved
milestones.
It counts what changed in the plan, not the days that passed.
.TP
.BI "pchart situation " PLAN
Where the plan stands: does the date hold, who waits on whom, what is next.
.TP
.BI "pchart why " "PLAN ITEM"
The chain of items that sets the date of
.IR ITEM .
.TP
.BI "pchart waits " PLAN
Every lane that waits on another lane, and for what.
.TP
.BI "pchart next " PLAN
What is due next, most urgent first.
.TP
.BI "pchart check " PLAN
Problems, warnings and hints.
Exit status 1 on warnings, 2 when a fixed date cannot be held.
.TP
.BI "pchart schedule " PLAN
Every calculated date, with what each item has to spare.
.TP
.BI "pchart holidays " "PLAN LANE"
The days off of a lane while the plan runs.
.TP
.BI "pchart set " "PLAN ITEM " "\fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
Change an item:
.BI \-\-duration " DAYS" ,
.BI \-\-on " DATE" ,
.BI \-\-no\-earlier\-than " DATE" ,
.BI \-\-no\-later\-than " DATE"
or
.BR \-\-calculated ,
.B \-\-done
or
.BR \-\-not\-done ,
.B \-\-buffer
or
.BR \-\-no\-buffer ,
.B \-\-important
or
.BR \-\-not\-important ,
.BI \-\-name " NAME" ,
.BI \-\-lane " LANE" ,
.BI \-\-who " WHO" ,
.BI \-\-share " PERCENT"
(1 to 100, else all of their time; it counts only for how busy they are, never for dates) and
.BI \-\-note " TEXT" .
.TP
.BI "pchart add " "PLAN ID " "\-\-lane " "LANE " "\-\-name " NAME " \fR([\fB\-\-duration \fIDAYS\fR] [\fB\-\-buffer\fR] | \fB\-\-milestone\fR) [\fB\-\-after \fIID,ID\fR] [\fB\-\-on \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-who \fIWHO\fR]"
Add an item.
Work without
.B \-\-duration
has no length yet; the plan has no dates until every piece of work has one.
.TP
.BI "pchart remove " "PLAN ITEM"
Remove an item that nothing waits on.
.TP
.BI "pchart link " "PLAN FROM TO"
Let
.I TO
wait on
.IR FROM .
.TP
.BI "pchart unlink " "PLAN FROM TO"
.I TO
no longer waits on
.IR FROM .
.TP
.BI "pchart apply " "PLAN EDITS.json"
Apply a JSON list of edits, all of them or none.
.B \-
reads the list from standard input.
See
.BR EDITS .
.TP
.BI "pchart export " PLAN " \fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
A view as pictures and PDF.
.B \-\-view
is
.I roadmap
(the default),
.IR milestones ,
.IR gantt ,
.IR phases ,
.IR now\-next\-later ,
or, for how the plan is built without dates,
.IR structure ,
.I network
and
.IR matrix .
The roadmap is dark like the terminal, at a
.B \-\-level
.RI ( overview ,
.I standard
or
.IR full )
and a
.B \-\-size
.IR WxH ,
or a light 16:9 page with
.BR "\-\-style light" ;
the other views are light pages.
.BI \-\-svg " FILE" ,
.BI \-\-png " FILE"
and
.BI \-\-pdf " FILE"
write the files.
.BI \-\-md " FILE"
writes the plan as Markdown with the milestone chart as SVG next to it;
.BI \-\-dot " FILE"
as a Graphviz file, lanes as clusters and the deciding chain in bold.
.B \-\-audience
leaves out what the audience does not see:
.I management
sees no warnings, the
.I client
no warnings and not what single items have to spare;
.I agents
get the item ids in Markdown.
The default is
.IR team ,
which sees everything.
.TP
.BI "pchart bench " PLAN " \-\-frames " N " \-\-out " FILE
Inside a terminal: change an item
.I N
times and time every step, from the change to the picture in the terminal.
.TP
.BR "pchart help " [ \-\-json ]
Every command, option, exit code and edit; with
.B \-\-json
for programs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable output, with
.B """schema"": 1"
in it.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With a change: show what would happen and write nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-today " DATE"
Calculate from this day instead of today, so results repeat.
.TP
.BI \-\-holidays " FILE"
Holiday data instead of the bundled data: lines of
.IR REGION <TAB> YYYY\-MM\-DD <TAB> Name .
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
With the screen: a theme by name instead of the current Omarchy theme.
.SH EDITS
.B pchart apply
takes a JSON list of edits and makes them as one change, all or none.
Each edit is an object with an
.B op
and its fields:
.TP
.B duration
{"op": "duration", "item": ID, "days": N}
.TP
.B fix
{"op": "fix", "item": ID, "kind": "on" | "no_earlier_than" | "no_later_than", "date": "YYYY\-MM\-DD"}
.TP
.B unfix
{"op": "unfix", "item": ID}
.TP
.B link
{"op": "link", "from": ID, "to": ID}
.TP
.B unlink
{"op": "unlink", "from": ID, "to": ID}
.TP
.B add
{"op": "add", "item": {"id": ID, "lane": LANE, "name": NAME, "duration": "5wd" | "milestone": true, "after": [ID]}}
.TP
.B remove
{"op": "remove", "item": ID}
.TP
.B rename
{"op": "rename", "item": ID, "name": NAME}
.TP
.B lane
{"op": "lane", "item": ID, "lane": LANE}
.TP
.B done
{"op": "done", "item": ID, "done": true}
.TP
.B buffer
{"op": "buffer", "item": ID, "buffer": true}
.TP
.B who
{"op": "who", "item": ID, "who": NAME | null}
.TP
.B share
{"op": "share", "item": ID, "share": PERCENT | null}
.TP
.B note
{"op": "note", "item": ID, "note": TEXT | null}
.TP
.B important
{"op": "important", "item": MILESTONE, "important": true}
.TP
.B note_at
{"op": "note_at", "lane": LANE, "date": "YYYY\-MM\-DD", "note": TEXT | null}
.TP
.B phase
{"op": "phase", "phase": NAME, "until": ID}
.TP
.B add_lane
{"op": "add_lane", "lane": ID, "name": NAME}
.TP
.B rename_lane
{"op": "rename_lane", "lane": LANE, "name": NAME}
.SH THE PLAN FILE
A plan file is TOML.
It starts with
.B format
and
.BR name ,
and may name a
.B start
date.
.TP
.B [[lanes]]
A row of the roadmap, usually a team:
.BR id ,
.BR name ,
and optionally the
.B place
whose holidays it keeps (a country such as
.I CN
or a subdivision such as
.IR DE\-BE )
and the
.B city
shown beside it.
.TP
.B [[items]]
A piece of work or a milestone:
.BR id ,
.BR lane ,
.BR name ,
.B duration
in working days
.RI ( 25wd )
or weeks
.RI ( 3w ),
.B after
(the ids it waits on),
.BR milestone ,
a fixed date
.BR on ,
.B no_earlier_than
or
.BR no_later_than ,
.B buffer
(time held back before a fixed date),
.BR done ,
.B important
(a milestone drawn as a star),
.B who
does it, the
.B share
of their time it takes, and a
.BR note .
.TP
.B [[phases]]
A phase of the plan:
.BR name ,
the item it ends with,
.BR until ,
and a
.B short
name for when the whole one does not fit.
.TP
.B [[notes]]
A note at a day of a lane:
.BR lane ,
.B date
and
.BR text .
It stays on its day when the plan moves.
.TP
.B [[snapshots]]
How the plan stood on a day, kept by
.B t
or
.BR "pchart snapshot" .
A plan with snapshots is format 2, so that an older pChart refuses it instead of dropping them.
.PP
A short plan:
.PP
.RS
.nf
format = 1
name = "Customer portal v1"

[[lanes]]
id = "product"
name = "Product"
place = "DE\-BE"
city = "Berlin"

[[items]]
id = "requirements"
lane = "product"
name = "Requirements"
duration = "10wd"

[[items]]
id = "launch"
lane = "product"
name = "Launch"
milestone = true
after = ["requirements"]
on = 2027\-03\-01
.fi
.RE
.SH WORKSPACE
A folder with a
.I workspace.toml
is a workspace, a team: its people are shared by all its projects, so the checks look at them across
the projects.
Its projects are the plans next to
.I workspace.toml
and in its
.I projects/
folder.
Enter on the People screen of a plan outside a workspace makes the plan's folder one.
.PP
.I workspace.toml
names
.BR name ,
.B lead
(who answers reports; without one everyone may),
.B teams
as
.BR "[{ name, city }]" ,
and
.B people
as
.BR "[{ name, team, capacity, away = [{ from, to }] }]" ,
where
.B capacity
is how much of their time they can work on projects in percent, else all of it, and
.B away
the days they are not there.
A person belongs to the team whose name their
.B team
matches, as a lane name does.
.PP
.RS
.nf
name = "Acme"
lead = "Jonas Weber"
teams = [{ name = "Frontend", city = "Bangalore" }]
people = [
  { name = "Priya Nair", team = "Frontend", capacity = 80, away = [{ from = 2027\-01\-04, to = 2027\-01\-08 }] },
]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reports are files of their own in
.IR reports/ ,
so no two people write the same file.
The folder reaches the others however the team shares the workspace, such as Syncthing, Git or
Nextcloud; pChart has no network code.
.SH HOLIDAYS
Each lane keeps the holidays of its
.BR place .
The holidays of every country and subdivision python\-holidays knows, 2006 to 2051, are built into
pChart;
.B \-\-holidays
takes other data, and
.B pchart holidays
lists the days off of a lane.
.SH THEMES
pChart draws in the colours of the current Omarchy theme and follows it while it changes, at most
once a second.
Without Omarchy it draws in Labra.
.B \-\-theme
takes one of the themes it ships by name.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PCHART_NAME
Who uses pChart on this computer, as the people of a workspace name them: who reports, and whether
they may answer reports.
.TP
.B PCHART_TRACE
A file the screen writes every wake\-up to: picture requests, finished pictures, events.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Where pChart keeps the plans opened before, else
.IR ~/.local/state .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where pChart looks for
.IR pchart/name ,
else
.IR ~/.config .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/pchart/recent
The plans opened before.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pchart/name
Its first line names who uses pChart here, when
.B PCHART_NAME
does not.
.TP
.I export/
Next to a plan: the files written from the Export screen.
.TP
.IR workspace.toml ", " reports/
The workspace and its reports.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Fine.
.TP
.B 1
.B check
found warnings.
.TP
.B 2
.B check
found that a fixed date cannot be held.
.TP
.B 3
A usage error, or an edit that cannot be made.
.TP
.B 4
A file error.
.SH TERMINALS
pChart draws pictures in the terminal: kitty, Ghostty and foot.
It needs kitty graphics or sixel; other terminals are not supported.
.SH EXAMPLES
A new plan whose launch is fixed on 1 March, opened at once:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pchart new portal.pchart \-\-template new\-application \-\-target 2027\-03\-01
pchart portal.pchart
.fi
.RE
.PP
Where it stands, and why the launch is where it is:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pchart situation portal.pchart
pchart why portal.pchart launch
.fi
.RE
.PP
What a longer frontend would do, without writing it, then for real:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pchart set portal.pchart frontend \-\-duration 30 \-\-dry\-run
pchart set portal.pchart frontend \-\-duration 30
.fi
.RE
.PP
The milestone chart for management, as PDF:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pchart export portal.pchart \-\-view milestones \-\-audience management \-\-pdf milestones.pdf
.fi
.RE
.PP
In a workspace, a report for the project lead:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pchart report projects/portal.pchart frontend \-\-later 3 \-\-comment "The API changed" \-\-by "Priya Nair"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The README of pChart, and its plan,
.IR docs/PLAN.md ,
which records every decision about how pChart works and looks.
